Z||000003||Tom88gt||11-13-2001||08:37 PM||||The year???<P>1988 rotors are $50 from the Fiero Store.  But you can use Cavalier (I think) rotors on the rear for about $12 each.  Do a search for "1988 rotors".<P>1984-87 rotors are way cheaper.  $81 & $54 are way too much.  Find a new parts store to do business with.||||reg||1
Z||000004||fiero56||11-13-2001||09:43 PM||||I did brakes this spring on my Formula.<P>4 rebuilt calipers<BR>$70/each for the rear, $50/each for the front<BR>4 new rotors<BR>$50/each<BR>S.S. braided brake lines<BR>$90 from FieroStore<BR>Rebuilt master cylinder<BR>$40<BR>2 sets of organic brake pads<BR>$25<P>All prices were when I bought from AutoZone this spring.<BR>The Cavalier rotors are a joke, I looked into using them on the rear. One of the worst and IMO unsafe things to try I've heard of yet. I took a mic with me to measure them, and knew right then they weren't going on my car.<P>This car stops scary fast now. It scares me to drive my '86 Fiero with factory brakes, its so unnerving.<P>"If you cant' afford maintenance what are you doing with a car" has been my philosophy through life. It pisses some people off when I say that, but its how I see things.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Ted||11-13-2001||11:40 PM||||I'm sorry, I was in a hurry today and forgot the details. I have an '84 2m4. Its not that I can't afford it, its that I shop before I get it. I don't like to get ripped off and I am sure you feel the same way.||||reg||1
Z||000006||fiero56||11-14-2001||04:05 AM||||If your getting those from a parts store, then the prices you posted are a rip off. I would suggest looking elsewhere.<P>If your near the Dayton area, I have rotors in good condition that I will give you if you take them off my hands.||||reg||1
Z||000007||SKIDMARK||11-14-2001||11:56 AM||||Try Federated auto parts, at least in the Cleveland area. I got front rotors for my 85 for about $23 each. I don't know about the rear but would guess about the same price or cheaper. They did have to order them but it was only a day or two wait.<P>------------------<BR>White '85 4cyl coupe<BR>Black '86 v-6 SE<BR>'81 CB900F Super Sport||||reg||1
